1.0.3
https://github.com/CodyTolene/pip-boy-3000-holotapes/pull/90
- Added the expanded light-control session runner used by the new APP.JS state model.
- Added slow fade, dual-color controls, extra colors, and additional effects while preserving KEEP EFFECT + EXIT, RESTORE PIP-OS + EXIT, and cancel/rollback behavior.
- Removed the separate fade-speed row; EFFECT SPEED now controls slow fade and dual-color fade timing.
- Regenerated APP.MIN.JS and SESSION.MIN.JS so the installed holotape uses the updated code.

1.0.2
https://github.com/CodyTolene/pip-boy-3000-holotapes/pull/76
- Remove the old persistent/default-light approach that patched LED behavior across reboots. The new version has no boot loader, no saved startup state, no icon/image assets, and no LED.JSON, so reboot returns the Pip-Boy to normal as if the app was never running.
- RESTORE PIP-OS + EXIT now explicitly clears the session runner, removes the temporary Pip.fadeTo wrapper, clears the effect interval, restores normal Pip-OS amber/charge lighting, and exits cleanly. This fixed the earlier issue where LED behavior stayed active or broke normal lighting after exit/reboot.
- KEEP EFFECT + EXIT starts a small in-memory session runner only for the current powered session. It keeps the selected effect running after the app closes, but does not persist through reboot. It also watches for firmware LED-off fades during power-down and shuts itself down so the Pip-Boy can power off normally.
- The UI was updated from a long list of hardcoded modes into separate controls:
  - Effect
  - Color
  - Speed
  - Brightness
  - Keep Effect + Exit
  - Restore Pip-OS + Exit
- Added selectable effects and color switching on effects.

